# RUNTIME dependencies for the model service — the deployment manifest.
#
# This is the companion to requirements-ci.in, and the two cover deliberately different surfaces:
#
#   requirements-ci.in   the CI TEST surface. Installs the package --no-deps and adds only light
#                        deps, because CI mocks the model layer. Its own header says it "is not a
#                        runtime deployment manifest".
#   requirements.in      THIS file. The heavy ML stack CI never installs — torch, FlagEmbedding,
#                        sentence-transformers — which is precisely the part where an unpinned
#                        upstream release breaks the service. sentence-transformers 5.x changing
#                        `device="auto"` already did exactly that; scripts/modal_smoke.py exists
#                        because of it.
#
# Mirrors [project.dependencies] in pyproject.toml, which states the SUPPORTED RANGES (what the
# package declares it works with). This file exists to turn one point in those ranges into a
# reproducible, hash-verified install. Change a range there, recompile here.
#
# Regenerate (note the platform — see the header of requirements.txt for why):
#   uv pip compile requirements.in --generate-hashes --python-version 3.11 \
#     --python-platform x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu -o requirements.txt
